.TH RENAME 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
rename \- rename or move a filesystem entry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int rename(const char* " old_path ", const char* " new_path ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR rename ()
renames or moves the entry named by
.I old_path
to
.IR new_path .
Linux rename rules apply: an existing destination may be replaced
atomically, subject to file and directory restrictions.
The operation does not move entries between mounted filesystems.
Consult
.BR rename (2)
for complete replacement and symbolic\-link semantics.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged; \-1 on failure with
.B errno
set to the positive Linux error number.
.SH ERRORS
Possible errors include
.BR ENOENT ,
.BR EACCES ,
.BR ENOTEMPTY ,
and
.BR EXDEV .
Other Linux
.BR rename (2)
errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Include
.B <errno.h>
for error constants. Crunch
.B errno
is process\-wide, not thread\-local.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unlink (3crunch),
.BR rename (2)
